    "items": [
      {
        "id": "rem-qft-cutoff-vs-continuum-interaction",
        "kind": "remark",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Fixed finite-mode results do not establish a continuum limit",
        "reference": "items/rem-qft-cutoff-vs-continuum-interaction.md#Statement",
        "design_state": "Authored draft with complete local argument; independent review remains pending.",
        "dependency_level": 5,
        "deps": [
          "def-qft-regulated-polynomial-hamiltonian",
          "thm-qft-self-adjoint-regulated-interaction",
          "def-countable-choice"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-qft-regulated-polynomial-hamiltonian": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-qft-self-adjoint-regulated-interaction": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "In [[def-qft-regulated-polynomial-hamiltonian]], the regulator is one fixed\nfinite mode count $N$ and one fixed polynomial on $\\mathbb R^N$. The self-adjoint\nand compact-resolvent conclusions of\n[[thm-qft-self-adjoint-regulated-interaction]] concern that fixed Hilbert space\nand form realization. They assert no continuum or infinite-volume limit. Here\n“continuum limit” means a limit of a specified family of finite-regulator\nobjects as a cutoff parameter changes, together with an identified comparison\nspace and convergence notion. No such family or convergence structure is part\nof the two cited items. This scope note does not assert that a continuum limit\ndoes not exist.",
        "strategy": "**Proof technique:** direct.\n\n**Given:** [F1] and [F2].\n\n1.1 The hypotheses in [F1] specify a single integer $N$, a single coordinate space $\\mathbb R^N$, and a single potential $V$; they contain no indexed family with varying cutoff. [A1, F1, algebra]\n\n2.1 A convergence assertion for varying cutoffs requires at least a family of objects, a common comparison space or maps between the spaces, and a convergence relation. Neither those data nor a limiting object occur in [F1] or [F2]. Therefore the theorems establish only the stated fixed-$N$ operator properties. The absence of those hypotheses is not a proof of nonexistence of a limit in a separately specified model. [A1, F1, F2, step 1.1, algebra] ∎",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Gerald Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics, 2nd ed., §2.3, pp.76–83",
              "url": "https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~gerald/ftp/book-schroe/schroe2.pdf",
              "locator": "§2.3, printed pp.76–83: quadratic-form construction for a fixed operator domain and Hilbert space."
            },
            {
              "title": "Richard S. Laugesen, Spectral Theory of Partial Differential Equations — Lecture Notes, Chapter 8, pp.48–50",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1203.2344v1",
              "locator": "Chapter 8, printed pp.48–50: compactness and spectral conclusions for a fixed confining operator."
            }
          ]
        },
        "library": "mathematics",
        "proof_strategy": "direct"
      },
      {
        "id": "ex-qft-quartic-ground-energy-bound",
        "kind": "example",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "One-mode quartic ground-energy increment bound",
        "reference": "items/ex-qft-quartic-ground-energy-bound.md#Statement",
        "design_state": "Authored draft with complete local argument; independent review remains pending.",
        "dependency_level": 6,
        "deps": [
          "def-qft-regulated-polynomial-hamiltonian",
          "thm-qft-self-adjoint-regulated-interaction",
          "lem-qft-hermite-oscillator-research-supplier",
          "lem-qft-regulated-ground-variational-bound",
          "lem-qft-coercive-polynomial-form-domain",
          "thm-dominated-convergence",
          "thm-hilbert-space-fourier-expansion",
          "def-countable-choice",
          "cor-mean-value-theorem"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-qft-regulated-polynomial-hamiltonian": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-qft-self-adjoint-regulated-interaction": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-hermite-oscillator-research-supplier": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-regulated-ground-variational-bound": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-coercive-polynomial-form-domain": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-dominated-convergence": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-hilbert-space-fourier-expansion": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
